# Household / Duplicate / Membership-Level — Full Inventory

This is an OfficeFloor + Spring PetClinic. The `POST /api/owners` flow is a chain of single-responsibility functions wired in a YAML file; each mutates the not-yet-persisted `Owner`. Below is every relevant file with its current source.

---

## 1. Entity — `Owner`

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`

Relevant persisted columns (lines 64–86) and the derived identity key (lines 163–223):

```java
@Column(name = "household_id")
private String householdId;

@Column(name = "namesake_count")
private Integer namesakeCount;

@Column(name = "household_size")
private Integer householdSize;

@Column(name = "membership_level")
private Integer membershipLevel;

@Column(name = "possible_duplicate")
private Boolean possibleDuplicate;

@Column(name = "possible_duplicate_of")
private Integer possibleDuplicateOf;
```

The identity key (used for hard-duplicate detection) is **derived, transient**, built from telephone + email + householdId:

```java
@Transient
public String getIdentityKey() {
    String tel = this.telephone == null ? "" : this.telephone;
    String em = this.email == null ? "" : this.email;
    String household = this.householdId == null ? "" : this.householdId;
    return tel + "|" + em + "|" + household;
}
```

Plus standard getters/setters for `householdId`, `householdSize`, `membershipLevel`, `namesakeCount`, `possibleDuplicate`, `possibleDuplicateOf`.

---

## 2. How `householdId` is generated/assigned

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdId.java`

Key points:
- Runs **only when the request opts in with `sharesHousehold == true`** (early-return otherwise, leaving `householdId` null).
- Groups owners by **normalized last name + normalized address** (case-insensitive, whitespace-collapsed). Address normalization is delegated to `AddressNormalizer.normalize(...)`.
- If any existing household member already has a `householdId`, reuses it; otherwise computes a deterministic id via `stableId(lastName, address)` = **first 12 upper-case hex chars of SHA-256 over `lastName + "|" + address`**.
- Back-fills the id onto any pre-existing member that lacks one (calls `ownerRepository.save(member)`).

```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
    String address = AddressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress());

    List<Owner> household = new ArrayList<>();
    String existingId = null;
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(existing.getId())) {
            continue;
        }
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(AddressNormalizer.normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
            household.add(existing);
            if (existingId == null && existing.getHouseholdId() != null
                    && !existing.getHouseholdId().isBlank()) {
                existingId = existing.getHouseholdId();
            }
        }
    }

    String householdId = existingId != null ? existingId : stableId(lastName, address);
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner member : household) {
        if (member.getHouseholdId() == null || member.getHouseholdId().isBlank()) {
            member.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(member);
        }
    }
}
```
`stableId` uses `lastName + "|" + address`; `normalize` = trim + collapse whitespace + lower-case (Locale.ROOT).

**Important discrepancy for your edit planning:** the current code hashes **last name + address**, but the openapi doc-comment and the acceptance test describe **last name + postcode** (see sections 6 and 8). They are out of sync.

`AddressNormalizer` (used above): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AddressNormalizer.java`

---

## 3. Household size input to membership level

Two separate things: `householdSize` (snapshot count) and `membershipLevel` (which currently does NOT use household size — see below).

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHouseholdSize.java`

Counts owners sharing the new owner's `householdId` (including the new one). If no `householdId`, size = 1.

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String householdId = owner.getHouseholdId();
    if (householdId == null || householdId.isBlank()) {
        owner.setHouseholdSize(1);
        return;
    }
    int count = 1; // the owner being created
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(existing.getId())) {
            continue;
        }
        if (householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
            count++;
        }
    }
    owner.setHouseholdSize(count);
}
```

---

## 4. Membership level computation

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignMembershipLevel.java`

Currently based on **email presence + namesakeCount**, NOT household size. Starts at 1, +1 if email present, +1 if `namesakeCount == 0`, capped at 3.

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner) {
    int level = 1;
    String email = owner.getEmail();
    if (email != null && !email.isEmpty()) {
        level++;
    }
    Integer namesakeCount = owner.getNamesakeCount();
    if (namesakeCount != null && namesakeCount == 0) {
        level++;
    }
    owner.setMembershipLevel(Math.min(level, 3));
}
```

Note: If you want household size to feed membership level, that wiring does not exist today — `AssignMembershipLevel` takes only `@Val Owner owner` and reads `email` + `namesakeCount`. `householdSize` is already set on the owner by this point in the chain (see ordering in section 9), so it is available to read.

`AssignNamesakeCount` (feeds membership level): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignNamesakeCount.java` — counts existing owners with same first+last name (case-insensitive).

---

## 5. Duplicate detection

There are two distinct mechanisms.

### 5a. Hard duplicate → 409 reject
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique.java`

Rejects when the derived `identityKey` (`telephone|email|householdId`) exactly matches an existing owner's. Because telephone is in the key, same-household different-telephone owners are allowed.

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateIdentityException {
    String identityKey = owner.getIdentityKey();
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(existing.getId())) {
            continue;
        }
        if (identityKey.equals(existing.getIdentityKey())) {
            throw new DuplicateIdentityException(identityKey);
        }
    }
}
```

Escalation type: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityException.java` (extends `Exception`, message `"An owner with identity key '...' already exists"`).

Handler → 409: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/escalation/DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler.java` (builds a `ProblemDetail` with `HttpStatus.CONFLICT`).

Handler wiring: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/escalation/org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityException.yml`
```yaml
handle:
  class: org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.DuplicateIdentityExceptionHandler
```

### 5b. Soft duplicate → flag, still create
`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignPossibleDuplicate.java`

Flags (does not reject) when the new owner shares an existing owner's **last name (case-insensitive) + postcode** but has a **different telephone**. Sets `possibleDuplicate` = true and `possibleDuplicateOf` = lowest matching id.

```java
public void service(@Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    String lastName = owner.getLastName();
    String postcode = owner.getPostcode();
    String telephone = owner.getTelephone();

    Integer matchId = null;
    if (postcode != null && !postcode.isBlank()) {
        for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
            if (owner.getId() != null && owner.getId().equals(existing.getId())) {
                continue;
            }
            if (equalsIgnoreCase(lastName, existing.getLastName())
                    && postcode.equals(existing.getPostcode())
                    && !equals(telephone, existing.getTelephone())) {
                if (matchId == null || existing.getId() < matchId) {
                    matchId = existing.getId();
                }
            }
        }
    }
    owner.setPossibleDuplicate(matchId != null);
    owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(matchId);
}
```

---

## 6. DTOs (generated from OpenAPI) & related mapping

DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`, `OwnerDto`, `OwnerPageDto`) are **generated at build time from the OpenAPI spec** — no hand-written `.java` sources exist. Source of truth:

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/openapi.yml`

- `sharesHousehold` (lines 2075–2085): **write-only boolean** on `OwnerFields` (request input). Doc says: when omitted/false, creating an owner whose **last name and address** match an existing owner is rejected 409; when true, allowed. (Lives on `OwnerFields`, so it is on `OwnerFieldsDto`.)
- `OwnerFields.required` (lines 2086–2092): firstName, lastName, address, city, telephone.
- Read-only response fields on `Owner` (extends `OwnerFields`):
  - `householdId` (2151–2160) — doc says derived from **last name and address**.
  - `identityKey` (2161–2171) — `normalizedTelephone|email|householdId`.
  - `namesakeCount` (2172–2182).
  - `membershipLevel` (2183–2194) — min 1, max 3; doc: starts at 1, +1 email, +1 if namesakeCount 0, capped at 3.
  - `possibleDuplicate` (2221–2229) / `possibleDuplicateOf` (2230–2239).
  - Note: **`householdSize` is NOT exposed in openapi.yml** (it exists on the entity + DB only). If you want it in responses you must add it to the spec.

Mapper: `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/mapper/OwnerMapper.java`

Relevant: `toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto)` explicitly **ignores** `householdId`, `namesakeCount`, `householdSize` (and id, pets, customerCode, membershipNumber) — these are assigned later by the chain functions, not mapped from the request:

```java
@Mapping(target = "id", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "pets", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "customerCode", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "membershipNumber", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "householdId", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "namesakeCount", ignore = true)
@Mapping(target = "householdSize", ignore = true)
Owner toOwner(OwnerFieldsDto ownerDto);
```
`toOwnerDto` does not ignore membershipLevel/possibleDuplicate/householdId, so those flow to the response DTO by name (householdSize would only flow if the DTO had the field, which it does not).

`BuildOwner` (creates the entity from the request DTO): `/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/BuildOwner.java`.

---

## 7. Repository methods

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/repository/OwnerRepository.java`

No household-specific query methods. The household/duplicate functions all use `findAll()` and filter in Java. Available methods: `findByLastName(String)`, `findByLastName(String, Pageable)`, `findById(int)`, `findByTelephone(String)`, `findByEmail(String)`, `save(Owner)`, `findAll()`, `findAll(Pageable)`, `delete(Owner)`. (There is no `findByHouseholdId`, no `findByPostcode`.)

---

## 8. YAML wiring — the create chain order

`/home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/resources/officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`

Order relevant to household/duplicate/membership (each `next:` links to the following step):

```
... build
 -> assignCustomerCode
 -> assignHousehold          (AssignHouseholdId)
 -> ensureIdentityUnique     (EnsureOwnerIdentityUnique)   <- hard-dup 409
 -> assignHouseholdSize      (AssignHouseholdSize)
 -> assignNamesakeCount      (AssignNamesakeCount)
 -> assignPossibleDuplicate  (AssignPossibleDuplicate)     <- soft-dup flag
 -> assignMembershipLevel    (AssignMembershipLevel)
 -> assignMembershipNumber   (AssignMembershipNumber)
